Refactoring Report — BKN Pharmacy Chrome Extension v2.1
Generated: 2026-04-24  
Codebase: `rx_menu_all.zip`  
Extension: BKN Hospital Pharmacy Department — Chrome Extension (Manifest v3)
---
Executive Summary
The extension is a well-functioning MV3 Chrome extension for BKN Hospital pharmacy operations. It covers IV labeling, auxiliary sticker printing, IPD queue management, drug delivery automation, and report generation. The codebase is largely clean and well-commented, but several structural and maintainability issues merit attention before the project scales further.
Total source: ~7,500 lines across 6 JS files, 4 HTML pages, 3 CSS files.
---
1. Architecture Overview
```
manifest.json
├── background.js         — MV3 Service Worker (message bus, fetch proxy, Drive upload)
├── content_script.js     — Injected into all pages (MRD table, Drug Delivery, Dispense WB)
├── popup.html / popup.js — Extension popup (tabs, IPD queue, report generation)
├── iv_sticker.html / iv_sticker.js   — IV label printing system (HAD, PFS, ATB, Cytotoxic)
├── aux_sticker.html / aux_sticker.js — Auxiliary sticker system (Premix, Mixing labels)
└── welcome.html / welcome.js         — Onboarding page shown on install
```
Communication flows:
```
popup.js ──→ background.js (extFetch, sendToDrugDelivery)
           ──→ content_script.js (getMrdRows, getDataBySelector)
content_script.js ──→ background.js (drugDeliveryResult, drugDeliveryReady)
background.js ──→ content_script.js in drugTab (fillAndSubmit)
```
