2. Issues by Priority
🔴 HIGH — Security & Correctness
2.1 Hardcoded Google Apps Script URL in background.js (Line 113)
```js
// background.js:113 — CURRENT
const url = 'https://script.google.com/macros/s/AKfycbwk0PsLdtR7a37iEzMLS15YBUlw25UPp92IQYRy2sYRRU-3LFb17HSvBZsIjA_tGTvyYQ/exec';
```
Issue: The full public deployment URL for the Med Rec Google Apps Script is hardcoded. If the script is redeployed, the URL changes silently and the feature breaks. Rotating or revoking the URL requires a code change and re-publish.  
Recommendation: Move to `manifest.json` or a config module `config.js`, or fetch from `chrome.storage` on first run.
2.2 Hardcoded Google Drive Folder ID (background.js Line 152)
```js
parents: ['14U3kFKdaA0tFkyFqMt1sDRByuIerOMbk']
```
Issue: Drive folder ID is embedded directly. If the folder changes or is used in multiple environments, it requires a code edit.  
Recommendation: Add to a shared `CONFIG` constant object or `chrome.storage`.
2.3 Internal IP Hardcoded in Multiple Places
```js
// manifest.json
"http://10.134.10.91/*"
// background.js
const DRUGDELIVERY_URL_PART = '10.134.10.91:8809/drugdelivery/web/ipfill';
// content_script.js
if (location.hostname === '10.134.10.91')
```
Issue: The internal hospital IP appears in 3 separate files. A network change requires updating all three independently and risks inconsistency.  
Recommendation: Define a single shared constant (or config object) imported/referenced across all files.
---
🟠 MEDIUM — Maintainability & Code Quality
2.4 Embedded Drug/Staff Data in iv_sticker.js (~100 lines of inline JSON)
```js
const DEFAULT_DRUGS = [ /* 35+ drug objects hardcoded */ ];
const DEFAULT_STAFF = [ /* 38 staff objects hardcoded */ ];
```
Issue: Drug formulary and staff roster change regularly. Embedding them as JavaScript literals means every update requires a code edit. The data is also duplicated in spirit across `iv_sticker.js` and `aux_sticker.js` (separate `PREMIX_DB`, `MIXING_DB` arrays).  
Recommendation:
Move drug/staff data to `drugs.json`, `staff.json`, `premix_db.json`, `mixing_db.json` in `web_accessible_resources`.
Load at startup with `fetch(chrome.runtime.getURL('drugs.json'))`.
This allows data updates without code changes and enables future admin UI to edit the source files.
2.5 Premix Database Embedded in aux_sticker.js (~39 entries, Mixing ~15 entries)
Same issue as above. These two static datasets span ~100 lines and are pharmacy-specific reference data that will change over time.
2.6 No Shared Utility Module
The following helpers are duplicated or near-duplicated across files:
Utility	Defined in
`sleep(ms)`	`content_script.js` and `iv_sticker.js` (implicitly via `setTimeout`)
`showToast()`	`iv_sticker.js` and `aux_sticker.js` (separate implementations)
`openPrintWindow()`	`iv_sticker.js` and `aux_sticker.js`
Date formatting	`iv_sticker.js` and `aux_sticker.js` (separate `formatDate()` variants)
Recommendation: Extract a shared `utils.js` with common helpers. Load via `web_accessible_resources` or restructure as a module bundle.
2.7 popup.js is Oversized (1,522 lines, 6 distinct feature areas)
`popup.js` handles tab navigation, IPD queue, IV sticker triggering, aux sticker triggering, RT_COMMON_257 report, RT_COMMON_917 report, and stock picking. This violates the single-responsibility principle and makes the file difficult to debug.  
Recommendation: Split into:
`popup-tabs.js` — tab nav
`popup-ipd.js` — IPD queue
`popup-reports.js` — report generation
`popup-init.js` — entry point that imports the above
2.8 Legacy `jspdf.min.js` Alongside `jspdf.umd.min.js`
```
cdnjs/jspdf.min.js       (307 KB)
cdnjs/jspdf.umd.min.js   (419 KB)
```
Issue: Two versions of jsPDF are bundled (older `.min.js` + newer `.umd.min.js`). Both are included in `web_accessible_resources`. The older one appears to be a leftover from a previous implementation.  
Recommendation: Confirm which version is actively used (search for `jspdf.min.js` references vs `jspdf.umd.min.js`). Remove the unused one. Combined they add 726 KB to extension size.
2.9 Inline Styles Used Extensively in content_script.js
```js
Object.assign(btn.style, {
  marginLeft: '6px',
  padding: '2px 10px',
  // 10+ more properties...
});
```
Issue: Button styles for injected UI elements are set entirely via `Object.assign(style, ...)`. This is hard to maintain and cannot be overridden by CSS.  
Recommendation: Add injected styles to a content script CSS file (declared in `manifest.json` via `css` key under `content_scripts`) and use `classList` instead.
