🟡 LOW — Code Cleanliness
2.10 Commented-Out Selector in content_script.js (Line 25)
```js
const MRD_TABLE_SEL = 'md-card-content md-table-container';
  // 'body > div.full-height.ng-scope.layout-row > div > md-content > ...'
```
The old verbose selector is left in a comment. It adds noise without value.  
Recommendation: Remove dead commented selectors; use git history for reference.
2.11 `getDataByTag` / `getDataByTagTable` Handler Returns Empty Array in background.js
```js
if (msg.action === 'getDataByTag') {
  sendResponse({ data: [] });
  return false;
}
```
This is a no-op stub that always returns empty — it appears to be a legacy handler from when DOM queries were routed through the background worker.  
Recommendation: Remove from `background.js`. The live implementation is in `content_script.js`.
2.12 `welcome.js` is Nearly Empty (6 lines)
```js
// welcome.js — entire file
document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {});
```
The welcome page logic is entirely in `welcome.html` inline scripts. MV3 best practice is to move all logic into the `.js` file.  
Recommendation: Move `welcome.html` inline scripts to `welcome.js`.
2.13 `Thumbs.db` in `/images/`
A Windows thumbnail cache file (`images/Thumbs.db`, 20 KB) is included in the extension bundle and listed under `web_accessible_resources`.  
Recommendation: Delete from project and add to `.gitignore`.
